    <!-- Body -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          For most concrete paver patios and walkways, polymeric sand is worth the extra $60 to $200 it costs over plain sand, because it ends the yearly cycle of washed-out joints, weeds and ant hills. But regular sand still wins in a few clear situations, and it is a lot more forgiving to install.
        </p>

        <TopPick />

        <div id="at-a-glance" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Two Options at a Glance
          </h2>

          <p>
            Both products fill the gaps between pavers so the pavers lock together and do not shift. The difference is what holds the sand in place. Regular sand relies on friction and gravity, so rain, wind and foot traffic gradually move it. Polymeric sand contains a binder that hardens when wet, so the joint becomes firm and stays put.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Factor</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Regular joint sand</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Polymeric sand</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Price per 50 lb bag</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Roughly $5-$10</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Roughly $20-$55</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Weed resistance</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Poor</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Good, not perfect</td>
                  </tr>
